<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Prague bourse makes quarterly PX50 index revisions.</title>
<headline>Prague bourse makes quarterly PX50 index revisions.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Prague Stock Exchange (PSE) on Monday said it had changed three issues in its PX50 index as part of its regular quarterly revisions to the index.</p>
<p>A PSE statement said food and beverage maker Milo Olomouc a.s., heating utility Moravskoslezske Teplarny a.s. and steel maker Vitkovice a.s. would be included in the calculation of the capitalisation-weighted index as of January 6.</p>
<p>It added that aeronautics firm AERO a.s., ocean shipper Ceska Namorni Plavba a.s. and glass fibre maker Vertex a.s. had been removed from the index to make room for the three new entries.</p>
<p>SPT Telecom a.s., CEZ a.s. and Komercni Banka a.s. remain the top three issues in the index.</p>
<p>-- Alan Crosby, Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
